{
  "source": "Prompts/training-bias-1.mp4",
  "duration": 188.4531875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.02,
      "end": 1.88,
      "text": "How much should I study for my exam?"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.76,
      "end": 5.7,
      "text": "You ask three people you trust and get three different answers."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.38,
      "end": 8.1,
      "text": "Your science teacher says three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.72,
      "end": 11.68,
      "text": "Your mom tells you 30 minutes because you have to work tonight."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.38,
      "end": 15.04,
      "text": "And your best friend chimes in, studying is overrated."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.74,
      "end": 20.56,
      "text": "All three are giving you honest advice, but each person is drawing strictly from their"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.56,
      "end": 21.58,
      "text": "own lived experience."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.38,
      "end": 24.04,
      "text": "The teacher sees academic rigor."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.42,
      "end": 28.34,
      "text": "The parent sees a busy schedule, and the friend sees social time."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.34,
      "end": 33.42,
      "text": "The information you get is entirely bounded by the specific source you ask."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.98,
      "end": 36.14,
      "text": "Their perspective dictates the shape of the answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.04,
      "end": 38.06,
      "text": "You heard three perspectives."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.76,
      "end": 41.04,
      "text": "Imagine an AI learned from only one."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.7,
      "end": 46.14,
      "text": "Let's say we have an AI model that receives its study data exclusively from websites written"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.14,
      "end": 47.1,
      "text": "by science teachers."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.68,
      "end": 52.38,
      "text": "It never reads a schedule from a working parent, and it never analyzes a text from a student."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.86,
      "end": 56.92,
      "text": "When you ask that system how much you should study, it will output three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.7,
      "end": 62.94,
      "text": "This is training bias, because the model learned from sources that provided only a fraction"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.94,
      "end": 66.94,
      "text": "of the total picture, that incomplete data dictates its final output."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.7,
      "end": 70.38,
      "text": "This infographic shows how incomplete data limits AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.22,
      "end": 73.1,
      "text": "First mechanism shows up too often."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.8,
      "end": 78.76,
      "text": "AI processes three hours repeatedly across teacher websites, learning to default to it."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.48,
      "end": 81.28,
      "text": "Second mechanism gets left out."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.84,
      "end": 83.58,
      "text": "Working students don't appear in this data."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.14,
      "end": 87.8,
      "text": "Lacking examples of their prep, the AI's advice overlooks their reality."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.32,
      "end": 93.1,
      "text": "The AI isn't making a conscious choice to ignore working students or favorite teachers."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.62,
      "end": 99.24,
      "text": "Its outputs are strictly mechanical reflections of how often a piece of data appeared or didn't"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.24,
      "end": 100.42,
      "text": "appear in its training set."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.16,
      "end": 102.12,
      "text": "Let's apply this realistically."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.32,
      "end": 107.64,
      "text": "You ask an AI for successful entrepreneurs, and it generates 10 names."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.28,
      "end": 112.78,
      "text": "You look at the screen and realize, wait, why are all 10 in tech?"
    },
    {
      "start": 113.46,
      "end": 117.74,
      "text": "Your instinct is to figure out who else would make the list outside the technology sector."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.86,
      "end": 120.9,
      "text": "The list tells you which industry showed up."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.3,
      "end": 122.78,
      "text": "You'd need more evidence to know why."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.66,
      "end": 124.86,
      "text": "Pause the video right here."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.4,
      "end": 130.32,
      "text": "Think of one specific prompt you could type into the AI right now to test this suspiciously"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.32,
      "end": 130.94,
      "text": "one-sided list."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.78,
      "end": 133.02,
      "text": "Hit play when you have your idea."
    },
    {
      "start": 133.8,
      "end": 138.3,
      "text": "Spotting a skewed pattern is an important first step, but it's only the first step."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.3,
      "end": 142.42,
      "text": "You have to actively interrogate the tool to locate the boundaries of its knowledge."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.5,
      "end": 147.94,
      "text": "This board provides three specific prompts you can use to diagnose suspected bias in your"
    },
    {
      "start": 147.94,
      "end": 149.08,
      "text": "everyday AI outputs."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.32,
      "end": 152.4,
      "text": "First, what's missing from this answer?"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.14,
      "end": 156.84,
      "text": "Second, show me examples that don't fit the pattern you just gave."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.56,
      "end": 160.96,
      "text": "Third, answer again, leaving out the most famous examples."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.9,
      "end": 165.48,
      "text": "These follow-up prompts force the AI to search for less dominant information."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.12,
      "end": 168.4,
      "text": "However, they don't guarantee a perfect answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 169.06,
      "end": 174.4,
      "text": "If a specific viewpoint or demographic was entirely excluded from the original training"
    },
    {
      "start": 174.4,
      "end": 179.06,
      "text": "data, no amount of clever prompting can force the AI to generate it."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.82,
      "end": 181.98,
      "text": "AI learns from its training data."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.7,
      "end": 184.64,
      "text": "Bias in the data can shape the answer."
    }
  ],
